peration-dbus-proto/deploy/netmaker/rumqttd.toml` | rumqttd config (part of netmaker MQ) |\n| `/home/jeremy/git/operation-dbus-proto/enrollment.key` | Netmaker enrollment token JSON |\n\n### Environment variables used across the codebase\n\n| Variable | Where used | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NETMAKER_MASTER_KEY` | `adapters/netmaker.rs:53`, `idenhtity-provision-handoff.txt` | Bearer auth for Netmaker API |\n| `NETMAKER_TENANT_ID` | `incus-compose.yaml:40`, `compose.yaml:40` | `8e65205a-b167-45f1-8911-03e1af5d98bf` -- Pro tenant |\n| `NETMAKER_TOKEN` | `.repomix-md/op-plugins.md:5003` | Token value from config |\n| `NETMAKER_METRICS_TARGET` | `incus-compose.yaml:86`, `compose.yaml:86` | Prometheus metrics target |\n| `WG_INTERFACE=netmaker` | `op-cognitive-mcp/main.rs:51`, `deploy/s6/op-cognitive-mcp/run:4`, `.repomix/cli-chats/...` | Default WireGuard interface name |\n| `NETMAKER_SERVER` | `deploy/s6/wg-netmaker/run:6` | `netmaker.3tched.com` |\n| `NETMAKER_NETWORK` | `deploy/s6/wg-netmaker/run:7` | `ghostbridge` |\n| `LICENSE_KEY` | `incus-compose.yaml:39`, `compose.yaml:39` | Netmaker Pro license |\n| `INSTALL_TYPE=pro` | `incus-compose.yaml:38`, `compose.yaml:38` | Pro edition |\n\n---\n\n## 5. s6 Service Definitions Under `deploy/s6/`\n\n### `deploy/s6/wg-netmaker/` directory\n- **`run`** -- Shell script running `netclient daemon` (prefers `/usr/local/bin/netclient`, falls back to `/usr/bin/netclient`)\n- **`producer-for`** -- Contains `wg-netmaker-log`\n- **`dependencies.d/gbr-wg`** -- Depends on `gbr-wg` (WireGuard base service)\n- **`type`** -- (not read, but standard s6 type file)\n\n### `deploy/s6/droid-daemon/dependencies.d/wg-netmaker`\n- Dependency marker for the droid daemon on `wg-netmaker`\n\n### `deploy/s6/op-cognitive-mcp/run` (line 4)\n- `export WG_INTERFACE=\"${WG_INTERFACE:-netmaker}\"`\n\n---\n\n## 6. References in `net.rs` (the `net` plugin)\n\nIn `/home/jeremy/git/operation-dbus-proto/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/net.rs`:\n- **Line 398** -- Interface ports starting with `nm` are classified as role `\"netmaker\"`\n- **Line 453** -- Comment: \"Skip netmaker interfaces (nm-*) - they are managed by netclient\"\n- **Lines 461-467** -- Ports starting with `nm-` or `wg` are skipped during bridge port addition\n\n---\n\n## 7. Audit Findings (from `.repomix-md/audits.md`)\n\nThe audits file documents several issues in `netmaker.rs`:\n- **Line 69789-69790** -- Finding 2: Direct Command Invocation Failure due to Unescaped Shell Operators at lines 269-272\n- **Line 70026** -- Line 8: `use std::collections::HashMap` is unused\n- **Line 70037** -- `leave_network` at line 142 is `#[allow(dead_code)]` (completely unreferenced)\n- **Line 70570-70574** -- Shell operator syntax error at line 293 (`&&` within an argument array)\n- **Lines 70811-70814** -- Sequential commands via `Command::new` without shell interpreter at line 247\n- **Line 70924** -- Something at line 65\n- **Line 71249** -- Something at lines 291-294\n- **Line 71400** -- Something at line 122\n\n---\n\n## 8. Summary of Key Observations\n\n1. **There are exactly two Rust source files** implementing netmaker functionality: the state plugin (`netmaker.rs` in `op-plugins`) and the gRPC adapter (`netmaker.rs` in `op-grpc-adapters`).\n\n2. **The state plugin is self-registering** via `inventory::submit!` at line 672 of `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/netmaker.rs`.\n\n3. **There is no `schemas/plugin/netmaker.json`** -- unlike some other plugins that have standalone schema JSON files, netmaker''s schema is defined entirely in code via `netmaker_schema()`.\n\n4. **The deployment model** uses Incus containers with no NICs -- services bind `127.0.0.1` inside containers, exposed to the host via Incus proxy devices as Unix sockets under `/run/netmaker/`. The `wg-xray` container mounts this directory and routes inbound traffic to the sockets.\n\n5. **The netclient daemon** runs as an s6 service (`wg-netmaker`) and manages the WireGuard mesh interface (`netmaker` interface on the host, `nm-*` interfaces in the OVS classification).\n\n6. **Identity was originally sourced from the netmaker WG interface** but this has been flagged as architecturally wrong -- there is no local WG identity interface on this host; identity comes from the decoy VPS via xray header injection.\n</task_result>\n</task>","title":"Find netmaker configuration","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","sessionId":"ses_0b50dde15ffeiIVMOMejeSjJYV","model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1783668810223,"end":1783668905369}}},"time":1783668905369}');
