INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4af44d4d001Pwh4B8TlRTW4UH','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',256,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4af22228001tcT2ebOHEjeoZv","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4af1fa1c001qDKCAT2zK9wpa9","type":"tool","callID":"call_3844caa13e964f61b5781f1e","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Find all service/daemon binaries","prompt":"Search the codebase at /home/jeremy/git/operation-dbus-proto for all binary entry points and service definitions. Look for:\n\n1. All `[[bin]]` entries in Cargo.toml files under `crates/`\n2. All `main.rs` files\n3. All files under `crates/*/src/bin/`\n4. All service definition files under `deploy/` (s6 service configs, run scripts)\n5. Any systemd or s6 service files\n\nFor each binary found, report the file path and a brief description of what it does (from comments or code).","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_0b50dd730ffefLh26ogbX4f9kE\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is the complete consolidated report.\n\n---\n\n## BINARY ENTRY POINTS AND SERVICE DEFINITIONS\n\n### PART 1: RUST BINARY ENTRIES (crates with `[[bin]]` in Cargo.toml + auto-discovered bins)\n\nAll paths are under `/home/jeremy/git/operation-dbus-proto/`.\n\n---\n\n#### crate: `op-agents` — Secure agent registry and D-Bus agent implementations\n- **`dbus-agent`** — `crates/op-agents/src/bin/dbus-agent.rs`\n  Runs any agent type (python-pro, rust-pro, memory, context-manager, etc.) as a D-Bus service; registers on the session or system bus for LLM tool discovery.\n- **`op-agent-manager`** — `crates/op-agents/src/bin/dbus-agent-manager.rs`\n  Starts and manages ALL agents simultaneously as D-Bus services; the canonical supervisor for agent daemon sets.\n\n#### crate: `op-assistant-grpc` — gRPC gateway for self-hosted Assistant\n- **`op-assistant-grpc`** — `crates/op-assistant-grpc/src/bin/op-assistant-grpc.rs`\n  gRPC gateway routing calls through the on-host `operation.v1` gRPC server with Ghostbridge schema-tag header injection for Xray OpenFlow routing.\n\n#### crate: `op-chat` — Chat / LLM integration (auto-discovered)\n- **`op-chat`** — `crates/op-chat/src/main.rs`\n  Standalone op-chat MCP server + ChatActor daemon; listens for MCP/gRPC and wires CozoDB memory + Qdrant semantic search.\n- **`list_tools_client`** — `crates/op-chat/src/bin/list_tools_client.rs`\n  CLI test client that connects to a ChatActor and lists all available MCP tools (ListTools request).\n\n#### crate: `op-cognitive-mcp` — Cognitive MCP (memory, NotebookLM, Qdrant, CozoDB)\n- **`op-cognitive-mcp`** — `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/main.rs`\n  Universal gateway for ALL external clients; serves HTTP/SSE (port 3003) + gRPC (port 50052, tonic-web + server reflection) + D-Bus state.\n- **`rag-ingest`** — `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/bin/rag-ingest.rs`\n  CLI to embed repomix zip content into Qdrant via Voyage embeddings, with cost estimation and token budgeting.\n- **`op-cog-admin`** — `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/bin/op-cog-admin.rs`\n  Minimal admin CLI for the CozoDB store (`user-add`, `user-list` commands).\n\n#### crate: `op-dbus-mirror` — D-Bus projection of OVSDB/NonNet (auto-discovered)\n- **`ovs-dbus-init`** — `crates/op-dbus-mirror/src/bin/ovs-dbus-init.rs`\n  Event-driven D-Bus mirror that bridges OVSDB changes onto the D-Bus plugin surface.\n- **`verify_performance`** — `crates/op-dbus-mirror/src/bin/verify_performance.rs`\n  Performance benchmark that creates 16,000 D-Bus mirror objects and measures throughput.\n\n#### crate: `op-gemma` — Gemma routing brain\n- **`op-gemma`** — `crates/op-gemma/src/main.rs`\n  Subid-to-tag-to-OpenFlow/xray routing brain; reads subid registry from `/etc/ghostbridge/subid-registry.json` and writes `xray-routes.json` + `openflow-routes.json` to `/dev/shm/`.\n\n#### crate: `op-grpc-adapters` — gRPC adapter layer\n- **`op-grpc-adapters`** — `crates/op-grpc-adapters/src/main.rs`\n  Wraps mail, netmaker, MQTT, and other services behind a uniform Tonic gRPC interface with Ghostbridge identity headers and reflection.\n\n#### crate: `op-grpc-bridge` — Zero-trust gRPC bridge (\"The Shuttle\")\n- **`op-grpc-bridge`** — `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/bin/op-grpc-bridge.rs`\n  The Shuttle — zero-trust gRPC gateway enforcing the Absolute Base rule via GhostbridgeInterceptor. Reads IdentitySled from SHM; rejects all requests until a valid sled exists.\n- **`op-grpc-bridge-zeroclaw`** — `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/bin/op-grpc-bridge-zeroclaw.rs`\n  ZeroClaw Axum Host — HTTP/gRPC-Web schema server; serves the zeroclaw PluginSchema from sealed blob SHM over native gRPC (Unix socket) + gRPC-Web/HTTP (TCP).\n- **`dump-protos`** — `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/bin/dump-protos.rs`\n  Dumps all static `.proto` files and dynamically-generated plugin protos to a target directory for external tooling (e.g., Lovable).\n\n#### crate: `op-identity` — WireGuard identity, Identity Sled, shuttle (auto-discovered)\n- **`op-identity-sled`** — `crates/op-identity/src/bin/op-identity-sled.rs`\n  CLI for reading, writing, and inspecting the Identity Sled in SHM (`/dev/shm/plugin_schema.dat`).\n- **`op-sled-top`** — `crates/op-identity/src/bin/op-sled-top.rs`\n  Top-like live TUI (ratatui/crossterm) view of the Identity Sled''s 1:1 shared memory layout, with auto-refresh.\n- **`op-identity-shuttle`** — `crates/op-identity/src/bin/op-identity-shuttle.rs`\n  Runs the schema shuttle once: reads Identity Sled, stamps Ghostbridge footprint/trace into env, writes dynamic xray config to `/dev/shm/xray-ghostbridge.json`, and SIGHUPs xray.\n\n#### crate: `op-mcp` — Unified MCP Protocol Server\n- **`op-mcp-server`** — `crates/op-mcp/src/main.rs`\n  Unified MCP server supporting compact/agents/full/grpc modes with stdio, HTTP+SSE, WebSocket, and gRPC transports.\n- **`op-mcp-compact`** — `crates/op-mcp/src/compact_main.rs`\n  Compact MCP server in stdio mode; exposes five lazy meta-tools for discovering and executing system tools.\n- **`op-mcp-agents`** — `crates/op-mcp/src/agents_main.rs`\n  MCP Agents Server with stdio transport; exposes cognitive agent tools (memory, sequential_thinking, rust_pro, etc.) for Gemini CLI and other stdio-only clients.\n\n#### crate: `op-mcp-shim` — MCP stdio-to-gRPC reflection shim\n- **`op-mcp-shim`** — `crates/op-mcp-shim/src/main.rs`\n  MCP (stdio) to gRPC bridge driven entirely by server reflection; projects every unary RPC as an MCP tool dynamically with no rebuild needed.\n\n#### crate: `op-network` — Native OVSDB, OpenFlow, rtnetlink\n- **`op-of-controller`** — `crates/op-network/src/bin/op-of-controller.rs`\n  OpenFlow 1.3 controller for `ovsbr0`; listens on port 6653 and installs bidirectional flows between configured port pairs.\n- **`op-xdp-wg`** — `crates/op-network/src/bin/op-xdp-wg.rs`\n  **DEPRECATED** — XDP orchestration for the wg-xray Incus container. Xray now runs on the host; retained for historical reference and potential host-side adaptation.\n- **`op-ovsbr0-afxdp`** — `crates/op-network/src/bin/op-ovsbr0-afxdp.rs`\n  Attach/detach host uplink (`eth0`) to `ovsbr0` as an AF_XDP port and migrate the management IP to/from the OVS internal bridge interface.\n- **`op-ovsbr0-setup`** — `crates/op-network/src/bin/op-ovsbr0-setup.rs`\n  Ensures `ovsbr0` exists with `datapath_type=netdev` and adds ports; uses rovs crate family for direct OVSDB manipulation.\n\n#### crate: `op-openvswitch-daemon` — Pure D-Bus proxy for rovs primitives\n- **`op-openvswitch-daemon`** — `crates/op-openvswitch-daemon/src/main.rs`\n  **DEPRECATED** — Pure passthrough D-Bus proxy for rovs primitives (JSON-RPC + OpenFlow). Exposes two D-Bus object paths: `/org/opdbus/rovs/jsonrpc` and `/org/opdbus/rovs/openflow`.\n- **`ovs-attach`** — `crates/op-openvswitch-daemon/src/bin/ovs_attach.rs`\n  D-Bus client that calls `BringUpLoopback` and `AttachPort` for container bootstrap; discovers config from the D-Bus plugin tree.\n\n#### crate: `op-plugins` — Plugin registry + schema definitions\n- **`opblob`** — `crates/op-plugins/src/bin/opblob.rs`\n  Shell driver for the schema-to-blob-to-catalog-to-btrfs pipeline. Subcommands: `demo-seal`, `seal-shm`, `seal-plugins`, `inspect`, `catalog`, `btrfs-seal`, `keygen`.\n\n#### crate: `op-projection` — Schema Engine / projection server (auto-discovered)\n- **`projection_server`** — `crates/op-projection/src/bin/projection_server.rs`\n  Pure read-through D-Bus projection of the plugin tree; mounts at `org.opdbus.v1.plugins` and serves each plugin state from SHM projections. Exposes a `refresh()` D-Bus method.\n\n#### crate: `op-s6-systemctl` — systemctl-to-s6 command mapping\n- **`op-s6-systemctl`** — `crates/op-s6-systemctl/src/main.rs`\n  D-Bus daemon providing a `systemctl`-compatible interface that maps to s6/s6-rc operations (start, stop, restart, enable, disable, status, list-units, journalctl, etc.).\n- **`s6d`** — `crates/op-s6-systemctl/src/bin/s6d.rs`\n  D-Bus CLI client wrapper for the canonical S6 control-plane service; provides the `s6d` command for managing s6 services over D-Bus.\n\n#### crate: `op-services` — Systemd replacement with dinit backend\n- **`op-services`** — `crates/op-services/src/bin/op-services.rs`\n  System-wide service manager daemon; starts D-Bus + gRPC interfaces for managing services (dinit backend).\n- **`systemctl`** — `crates/op-services/src/bin/systemctl.rs`\n  `systemctl`-compatible CLI that talks to the `op-services` gRPC server (`[::1]:50053`) for service management.\n- **`systemctl-native`** — `crates/op-services/src/bin/systemctl-native.rs`\n  Native `systemctl`-compatible CLI that talks to the `op-services` D-Bus interface directly (no gRPC/network dependency).\n\n#### crate: `op-tools` — Tool registry and execution (auto-discovered)\n- **`op-packagekit-install`** — `crates/op-tools/src/bin/op-packagekit-install.rs`\n  CLI to install packages via the PackageKit D-Bus service (no CLI fallbacks).\n\n#### crate: `op-web` — Unified web server for op-dbus-v2\n- **`op-web-server`** — `crates/op-web/src/main.rs`\n  Unified HTTP API server + static UI for op-dbus-v2; consolidates all HTTP services and serves the shadcn React frontend.\n- **`opdbus`** — `crates/op-web/src/bin/opdbus.rs`\n  gRPC server for all Operation services; binds to the `ovsbr0` interface IP so all Incus containers can reach it through OVS.\n\n#### crate: `op-xray-daemon` — Xray D-Bus lifecycle manager\n- **`op-xray-daemon`** — `crates/op-xray-daemon/src/main.rs`\n  D-Bus daemon for managing the Xray proxy lifecycle (start, stop, restart, reload, status, get_config) via schema-driven D-Bus methods.\n\n---\n\n### PART 2: s6 SERVICE DEFINITIONS (`deploy/s6/`)\n\nEach service directory contains a `run` script and optionally metadata files (`type`, `notification-fd`, `pipeline-name`, `consumer-for`, `producer-for`, `down`).\n\n| Service | Run script path | Description |\n|---------|----------------|-------------|\n| **chatmanager** | `deploy/s6/chatmanager/run` | Standalone op-chat MCP server and actor daemon; listens on `OP_CHAT_LISTEN` (default :50053) |\n| **dbus-session** | `deploy/s6/dbus-session/run` | Starts a D-Bus session bus daemon (`busd`) at `$DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS` |\n| **droid-daemon** | `deploy/s6/droid-daemon/run` | Droid factory daemon (runs `droid daemon`) |\n| **gbr-warp** | `deploy/s6/gbr-warp/run` | Cloudflare WARP WireGuard tunnel — middle hop in the GhostBridge privacy chain |\n| **gbr-wg** | `deploy/s6/gbr-wg/run` | WireGuard entry point for the GhostBridge privacy chain (`wg0`) |\n| **gbr-xray** | `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/run` | Xray REALITY egress for the GhostBridge privacy chain |\n| **gemma** | `deploy/s6/gemma/run` | Default routing loop — reads registry, drives D-Bus routing plugin, runs shuttle |\n| **netmaker-rumqttd** | `deploy/s6/netmaker-rumqttd/run` | MQTT broker (`mosquitto`) for Netmaker mesh communication |\n| **op-assistant-grpc-srv** | `deploy/s6/op-assistant-grpc-srv/run` | gRPC gateway for the self-hosted Assistant; targets op-grpc-bridge |\n| **op-cli-notebook-logger** | `deploy/s6/op-cli-notebook-logger/run` | Syncs CLI NotebookLM logs to Google Drive |\n| **op-cognitive-mcp** | `deploy/s6/op-cognitive-mcp/run` | Cognitive MCP server with CozoDB memory and Qdrant semantic search |\n| **op-dbus-mirror** | `deploy/s6/op-dbus-mirror/run` | D-Bus mirror of OVSDB state onto the D-Bus surface |\n| **op-grpc-bridge** | `deploy/s6/op-grpc-bridge/run` | The Shuttle — zero-trust gRPC bridge running `op-grpc-bridge` |\n| **op-grpc-bridge-zeroclaw** | `deploy/s6/op-grpc-bridge-zeroclaw/run` | Zeroclaw Axum Host — gRPC/gRPC-Web schema bridge for containers |\n| **op-mcp-compact** | `deploy/s6/op-mcp-compact/run` | Compact MCP server (5 lazy meta-tools) for loopback chatbot |\n| **op-nlm-sync-drive** | `deploy/s6/op-nlm-sync-drive/run` | Periodic Google Drive sync for NotebookLM data |\n| **op-openvswitch-daemon** | `deploy/s6/op-openvswitch-daemon/run` | **DEPRECATED** — D-Bus proxy for rovs OVSDB/OpenFlow primitives |\n| **op-projection** | `deploy/s6/op-projection/run` | Projection server — read-through D-Bus tree of plugin states from SHM |\n| **op-web-srv** | `deploy/s6/op-web-srv/run` | Unified op-web-server HTTP API + static UI |\n| **opdbus** | `deploy/s6/opdbus/run` | Hypervisor WireGuard identity tunnel to Oracle VPS (`wg0`) |\n| **wg-decoy** | `deploy/s6/wg-decoy/run` | WireGuard decoy tunnel to Oracle VPS (identity ingress) |\n| **wg-netmaker** | `deploy/s6/wg-netmaker/run` | Netmaker WireGuard mesh network (`netclient daemon`) |\n| **wg-opdbus** | `deploy/s6/wg-opdbus/run` | Stub — WireGuard managed by the plugin registry |\n| **zeroclaw** | `deploy/s6/zeroclaw/run` | Antigravity/ZeroClaw gateway (host-native) |\n| **zeroclaw-routing-uigen** | `deploy/s6/zeroclaw-routing-uigen/run` | Grok-backed routing/UI proposal agent; periodically asks LLM for JSON routing proposals |\n| **zeroclaw-wayland** | `deploy/s6/zeroclaw-wayland/run` | Isolated headless Wayland compositor (weston) for zeroclaw-gui |\n| **zeroclaw-wayvnc** | `deploy/s6/zeroclaw-wayvnc/run` | VNC view into the isolated headless Wayland compositor |\n| **zeroclaw-wgui** | `deploy/s6/zeroclaw-wgui/run` | Zeroclaw GUI pinned to the isolated Wayland socket |\n\nEach service also has a corresponding `-log/` service for s6 log capture (e.g., `gbr-xray-log/`, `op-grpc-bridge-log/`, `op-web-log/`, etc.).\n\n---\n\n### PART 3: SYSTEMD SERVICE FILES (`deploy/systemd/`)\n\n| File | ExecStart | Description |\n|------|-----------|-------------|\n| `deploy/systemd/op-dbus.service` | `/usr/local/sbin/op-dbus` | OP-DBUS Main Service (legacy) |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-web.service` | `/usr/local/sbin/op-web-server` | OP-Web Server (MCP Control Center) |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-web.service.journal` | `/usr/local/sbin/op-web-server` | Variant op-web service with journald logging |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-mcp.service` | `op-mcp-server --mode full --http 0.0.0.0:3001` | Full MCP Protocol Server |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-mcp-compact.service` | `/usr/local/sbin/op-mcp-compact` | Compact MCP Server |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-mcp-agents.service` | `op-mcp-server --mode agents` | MCP Agents Server |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-agents.service` | `/usr/local/sbin/op-agent-manager` | D-Bus Agent Manager |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-dbus.target` | — | Target grouping op-web + op-mcp as a stack |\n| `deploy/systemd/mcp-smart-gateway.service` | `mcp-smart-gateway --http` | MCP Smart Gateway (HTTP mode) |\n| `deploy/systemd/op-cli-notebook-log-sync@.service` | `op-cli-notebook-log-sync.sh` | Per-instance CLI NotebookLM log sync |\n| `deploy/systemd/streaming-logs.service.root` | `streaming-logs-admin` | Streaming Logs Admin Service |\n| `deploy/systemd/networkd/*.network` | — | systemd-networkd configs for OVS, WireGuard, Xray, gRPC bridge interfaces |\n\n---\n\n### PART 4: s6-RC SERVICE DIRECTORIES (`deploy/services/`)\n\n| File | Command | Depends-on | Description |\n|------|---------|------------|-------------|\n| `deploy/services/boot` | *(internal)* | — | s6-rc boot marker |\n| `deploy/services/op-session-bus` | `/home/jeremy/.../deploy/bin/op-session-bus` | — | Session D-Bus daemon |\n| `deploy/services/op-dbus` | `/home/jeremy/.../deploy/bin/op-dbus` | `op-session-bus` | Main op-dbus daemon |\n| `deploy/services/op-web` | `/usr/local/sbin/op-web-start.sh` | `op-dbus` | Web server |\n| `deploy/services/op-projection` | `/home/jeremy/.../deploy/bin/projection_server` | `op-dbus` | Projection server |\n| `deploy/services/op-chat` | `/home/jeremy/.../deploy/bin/op-chat` | `op-web` | Chat daemon |\n| `deploy/services/op-services` | `/home/jeremy/.../deploy/bin/op-services` | `op-web` | Service manager |\n\n---\n\n### PART 5: GHOSTBRIDGE SYSTEMD USER FILES (`deploy/ghostbridge/`)\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `deploy/ghostbridge/op-dbus.socket` | systemd user socket unit for GhostBridge session socket (`%t/op-dbus.sock`) |\n| `deploy/ghostbridge/openbox.target` | systemd user target for Openbox window manager session |\n| `deploy/ghostbridge/save-sessions` | Bash script to save GhostBridge sessions to disk on shutdown/reboot |\n| `deploy/ghostbridge/session-manager.py` | Python session manager for GhostBridge |\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY\n\nTotal Rust binary entry points: **41**\n- 31 explicitly declared in `[[bin]]` sections\n- 10 auto-discovered in `src/bin/` directories (crates without `[[bin]]`)\n\nTotal s6 service definitions: **28** run scripts under `deploy/s6/` plus their log services\nTotal systemd service files: **11** `.service`/`.target` files under `deploy/systemd/`\nTotal s6-rc service definitions: **6** config files under `deploy/services/`\nTotal GhostBridge service files: **3** systemd units + 2 scripts under `deploy/ghostbridge/`\n</task_result>\n</task>","title":"Find all service/daemon binaries","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","sessionId":"ses_0b50dd730ffefLh26ogbX4f9kE","model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1783668811987,"end":1783668952397}}},"time":1783668952397}');
