INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4af66840001o2oi9oF9GPToTs','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',309,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4af65c9b001qJfUaEMM7DgWOR","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4af63ca0001P0kMUCGXWePFl3","type":"reasoning","text":"The user is asking about their WireGuard identity or OVSDB identity - they mentioned ports showing on `ip a` but not via OVS D-Bus commands. Let me re-read their original question and look at the OVS D-Bus code more carefully to find where the issue might be.\n\nActually, I think they might be asking about whether I can see their system''s identity/sessionid - from the CLAUDE.md: \"Identity = WireGuard pubkey → Argon2(PSK, salt=pubkey) sessionid; a container''s name IS its sessionid.\"\n\nBut wait - they might also be asking about the D-Bus daemon''s identity check - whether the `op-openvswitch-daemon` can verify who''s calling. Let me look at the daemon''s `transact` method and see if there''s any identity/session verification that might be blocking access.\n\n\nThe daemon might be rejecting connections due to identity verification, or the ports could be filtered out based on some permission check. I need to examine the actual OVS D-Bus query code and the daemon''s access control logic to understand what''s happening.","time":{"start":1783669087387,"end":1783669090368}},"time":1783669090368}');
