INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4afb9ed5001xxY4TFPt7n47Ox','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',586,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4afb8c8c001m14Vy6QLiIwR0o","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4afb73ba001zU7E6pICmB7ZzJ","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me answer the user''s questions:\n\n1. **Identity sled**: Not running. The `identity_sled.json` projection shows `{\"sleds\":[]}` - empty sleds array. The cognitive MCP logs warn: \"Could not read WireGuard public key — identity sled not written; set WG_PUBKEY env var to override\"\n\n2. **Container matching UUID**: The incus container `9431b9db-0e5d-f895-f43e-226352d30c8a` is RUNNING but has no IP. This could be the zeroclaw workspace container.\n\n3. **Covsw controller on 10.200.0.1**: Looking at the `ss` output:\n   - `10.200.0.1:8444` - CozoDB listening\n   - `10.200.0.1:50051` - gRPC bridge (op-grpc-bridge) listening\n   - `10.200.0.1:53` - DNS\n\nWait, the user asked \"is the covsw controller declared as 10.200.0.1 on the bridge\" - I think they mean CozoDB controller. Let me check what `10.200.0.1` actually is. From the zeroclaw.json, `grpc_target: \"http://10.200.0.2:50051\"` - so 10.200.0.2 is what zeroclaw expects for gRPC. But 10.200.0.1:50051 is listening on the host side.\n\nLet me check what bridge this is - probably the bridge interface.","time":{"start":1783669427340,"end":1783669432021}},"time":1783669432021}');
