INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4afdb522001A0Q6VpLnogY1Io','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',745,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4afda368001cI0GCokbdg41SA","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4afd8a180019i8ao697XfVZjh","type":"reasoning","text":"The user is telling me:\n1. `identity_sled.dat` is deprecated\n2. The actual container IS the sled now\n\nSo the identity model has changed - instead of a separate identity sled file/binary, the container itself IS the identity sled. This is a significant architectural shift.\n\nLet me understand what this means for the codebase and the questions we''ve been investigating. The `op-identity-sled` binary and its projection (`identity_sled.json`) are deprecated. The container''s identity is now its WireGuard pubkey → sessionid derivation, and the container itself IS the sled.\n\nThis also means the `identity_sled_dispatch` in the gRPC bridge may be dealing with deprecated concepts.\n\nLet me continue investigating the current state - specifically:\n1. What does the `identity_sled_dispatch` actually do now?\n2. What''s the current OVS D-Bus path (since `OvsdbDbusClient` is deprecated)?\n3. Where are the direct `rovs` D-Bus calls happening?\n\nLet me focus on what''s actionable - the user said \"Continue if you have next steps.\" The next steps from before were:\n1. Find where the new direct `rovs` D-Bus calls are (since `OvsdbDbusClient` is deprecated)\n2. Fix the port parsing bug in `grpc.rs:283`\n3. Understand the new identity model\n\nLet me check what the new `rovs` D-Bus path looks like - if `OvsdbDbusClient` is deprecated, what replaced it?","time":{"start":1783669564265,"end":1783669568802}},"time":1783669568802}');
