INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4afe3f3a001ji9JTlqQ1FdBKX','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',778,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4afe2735001aixGB7F7yqKBRp","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4afde510001HxUFlkcFJrYEV7","type":"text","text":"Good. Now I have a clear picture. Let me summarize the architectural state as I understand it:\n\n**Deprecated (dead code paths):**\n- `op-network/src/rovs_proxy.rs` — `OvsdbDbusClient`\n- `op-openvswitch-daemon` — entire crate\n- `op-dbus-mirror` — still imports `OvsdbDbusClient` in 3 files\n- `op-identity-sled` binary + `identity_sled.json` projection\n- `identity_sled.dat` / `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/identity_sled.json`\n\n**Current architecture:**\n- `rovs_commands` plugin (schema-only) → gRPC bridge `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` → direct `rovs` D-Bus calls\n- Container IS the sled — `identity_sled_dispatch.rs:1` confirms: \"the container is the sled is the identity\"\n- Sled state persists to Cozo (`identity_sleds` / `session_events` relations)\n- `provision_container` creates Incus instance + writes sled in one mutation\n\n**What I''m unsure about:**\n\n1. `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` at `mutation_engine.rs:1212` still takes `OvsdbDbusClient` — is this the deprecated path, or is it being actively migrated?\n2. `op-dbus-mirror` still references `OvsdbDbusClient` — is this crate fully deprecated or still in use?\n3. Is the port visibility issue (`list_ports` not showing ports) still relevant, or does the new `rovs` direct path handle this differently?","time":{"start":1783669598005,"end":1783669604153}},"time":1783669604154}');
