INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b002936001JCXZCiR0iOhqeT','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',885,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b001cd5001wmJYmha8wMtRMy","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b00082e00166SwEkUJDqyOCb","type":"reasoning","text":"The user is correcting me - they said \"rovs commands are not schema only, they have a sealed blob\" and now \"backed by schema\". So the `rovs_commands` plugin IS a sealed blob in SHM (`rovs_commands.e359cd0c2cc3b1eb.blob` exists), and the execution path goes through `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` in `mutation_engine.rs` which uses the deprecated `OvsdbDbusClient`. The user is telling me the blob is backed by schema - meaning the plugin has a real sealed blob with schema, not just a schema-only stub.\n\nSo the architecture is:\n1. `rovs_commands` plugin has a sealed blob in SHM (confirmed: `rovs_commands.e359cd0c2cc3b1eb.blob`)\n2. It has a schema defined in `rovs_commands_schema()` \n3. Execution goes through `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` which still uses `OvsdbDbusClient`\n\nThe user said \"rovs commands called directly, with `method_transact`\" - so the intent is that the rovs commands should be called via D-Bus `PluginService.CallMethod` (the standard plugin method call path), not through the deprecated `OvsdbDbusClient`.\n\nLet me trace the call path at line 906 more carefully to understand the full dispatch.","time":{"start":1783669726421,"end":1783669729589}},"time":1783669729590}');
