INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b070ef4001WrUkNgDT5Xuirz','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1132,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b06fe8b001cIjPKVfdBVM0t0","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b06f684001CsSEf7wXW08PNL","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me analyze the new information from the conversation and update the summary accordingly.\n\nKey new info:\n1. The user confirmed the refactor \"really worked and was beautiful\" - container was the identity, no loop devices, no run directories, btrfs was linked to Cozo via `btrfs device add` to the container\n2. Git commits checked - latest commit is `40f5551c identity_sled: fix provision_container instance defaults + error visibility`\n3. The diff analysis shows:\n   - `gemma_brain.rs` was **deleted** (384 lines removed) - this was a planned deletion\n   - New `routing.rs` and `routing_dispatch.rs` files are uncommitted\n   - `jsonrpc_interface.rs` had dead duplicate code removed (57 lines of orphaned struct/impl blocks after the main impl)\n   - `event_dispatcher.rs` removed stale `MirrorEvent::NonNet` match arm\n   - `mutation_engine.rs` added routing dispatch support (both in mutate and dispatch paths)\n   - Various cleanup: removed unused imports from identity, cognitive MCP interceptor expanded   - Deploy scripts modified for gemma s6 service - `mod.rs` and `plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs`: removed `gemma_brain`, added `routing`\n\nThe user is asking me to check what should have been deleted that corresponded to the change. The `gemma_brain.rs` was deleted, and there''s the corresponding cleanup in `mod.rs` and `plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs`. The `NonNet` match arm was removed from event_dispatcher.rs. The dead code in `jsonrpc_interface.rs` was removed.\n\nLet me update the summary with these findings.","time":{"start":1783670177420,"end":1783670181620}},"time":1783670181620}');
