INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b0a39c4001lXKo3eV5IVrCX5','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1271,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b0a2aae001eQkCoQu4F5LUlE","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b0a051e00130mS6J3LBzGafs","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me understand the current state:\n\n1. **gemma**: An s6 longrun service in `/etc/s6/sv/gemma` (symlinked from `deploy/s6/gemma`). It runs a routing loop that calls `zcall routing derive/publish` or falls back to `op-gemma`. It has a dependency in `gbr-xray/dependencies.d/gemma`.\n\n2. **ollama**: An s6 longrun service in `/etc/s6/sv/ollama` (not a symlink, real directory). There''s also `ollama-srv` which is similar.\n\n3. **gbr-xray**: Depends on `gemma` (via `dependencies.d/gemma`). The xray run script exits if `/etc/xray/config.json` doesn''t exist.\n\nThe user wants:\n1. gemma and ollama to NOT start at boot\n2. A minimal xray config to be available if the inference model isn''t up\n\nLet me check:\n- What dependencies does gbr-xray have?\n- What''s the current xray config situation?\n- How to disable services in s6 (usually by creating a `down` file or removing them from the bundle)","time":{"start":1783670385326,"end":1783670389188}},"time":1783670389188}');
