INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b0ed35a001SUICjda5cIAe2S','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1582,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b0ec4bb001CS6DHldcxJ5C0S","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b0ea565001KoEUoAnyy19eTs","type":"reasoning","text":"The user is giving me an important update: incus storage pools are now btrfs devices in CozoDB. This means the storage pool management is being tracked in the CozoDB graph store, not just via incus CLI. This is consistent with the op-dbus architecture where CozoDB is the state store.\n\nLet me update the summary with all the new findings:\n\n1. **btrfs-pool is mounted and accessible**: `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool` IS mounted (bind mount from `/opt/incus/storage-pool`). So the qdrant container error about missing storage path is NOT a mount issue - the pool exists.\n\n2. **netclient in netmaker-pro**: confirmed working - netclient is at `/usr/local/bin/netclient`, systemd `enabled`, running as daemon (PID 803). This is the UIX socket-modified version the user mentioned.\n\n3. **qdrant storage issue**: The error was `Failed to handle idmapped storage: No such file or directory: \"/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/rootfs\"` - but the btrfs-pool IS mounted. The issue is likely that the container''s btrfs subvolume was deleted/lost from the pool. Need to check if the subvolume exists under `/opt/incus/storage-pool/containers/qdrant/`.\n\n4. **xray config**: needs sudo to fix the broken symlink.\n\n5. **New info**: Incus storage pools are now btrfs devices in CozoDB - this means CozoDB tracks the storage infrastructure.\n\nLet me proceed with fixing things.","time":{"start":1783670686907,"end":1783670690650}},"time":1783670690650}');
