INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b128a75001eR7Z9pZFd28yPy','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1842,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b12631e001YnWUWAXJvnULON","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b124bc9001IXN2h4luEzU4Qh","type":"reasoning","text":"OK so the qdrant storage volume exists in CozoDB (btrfs-pool), but the actual btrfs subvolume on disk doesn''t match. The incus metadata lists `qdrant` as a container volume with `578a6e31-891e-e20c-9374-8a5138bffb9f` as a UUID-named subvolume.\n\nWait - looking at the btrfs subvolume list, the UUID-named subvolumes are:\n- `4991a337...`\n- `578a6e31...`- `9431b9db...`\n\nAnd the `incus storage volume list` shows:\n- `578a6e31-891e-e20c-9374-8a5138bffb9f`\n- `4991a337-d418-c9ab-aa3f-2d9ab272471c`\n- `9431b9db-0e5d-f895-f43e-226352d30c8a`\n- `assistant`\n- `cozo`\n- `mail-3tched`\n- `qdrant`\n\nSo qdrant exists as a volume in incus storage, but the subvolume path `containers/qdrant` (the old-style named path) doesn''t exist as a btrfs subvolume. The UUID-named subvolumes are the ones that exist.\n\nActually wait - the containers subdirectory has the qdrant dir but it''s not a btrfs subvolume. The UUID-named ones are the subvolumes. But which UUID corresponds to which container?\n\nLet me check the incus container metadata to find which UUID is qdrant''s.\n\nActually, looking at the btrfs subvolume paths:\n- `containers/4991a337-d418-c9ab-aa3f-2d9ab272471c`\n- `containers/578a6e31-891e-e20c-9374-8a5138bffb9f`\n- `containers/9431b9db-0e5d-f895-f43e-226352d30c8a`\n\nThe `incus storage volume list` also shows `578a6e31`, `4991a337`, `9431b9db` plus `assistant`, `cozo`, `mail-3tched`, `qdrant`.\n\nWait, the named volumes (`assistant`, `cozo`, `mail-3tched`, `qdrant`) are also listed but NOT as btrfs subvolumes. The UUID ones are the actual btrfs subvolumes.\n\nHmm, actually incus uses two naming schemes - the older named containers become btrfs subvolumes as `containers/<name>`, and newer ones use UUID-based names. The fact that we have both suggests a mix.\n\nBut the `btrfs subvolume delete` failed on `containers/qdrant` saying it''s not a btrfs subvolume, so it''s just a plain directory. And the btrfs subvolume list only shows UUID-named paths.\n\nSo the qdrant volume exists in incus''s storage DB but the underlying subvolume is broken/missing. Let me look at what''s in the `containers/qdrant` directory - maybe it''s just a regular directory with leftover files.\n\nActually, I can''t `ls` it due to permissions. Let me try with sudo.\n\nAlso, the user wants me to:\n1. Fix qdrant (get it working again)\n2. Make sure qdrant advertises gRPC instead of/in addition to HTTP\n\nLet me look at what qdrant config currently looks like inside the container, and figure out how to fix the storage.","time":{"start":1783670924062,"end":1783670934133}},"time":1783670934133}');
