INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b13a101001BqJPQhNh9lnemU','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1921,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b139003001eEY6DxQ8Ul2N6b","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b1374b3001eyH6wLXgE38LiM","type":"reasoning","text":"The user is telling me:\n\n1. \"it isnt in pqdrant\" - meaning the qdrant data isn''t in the qdrant container (probably it''s in CozoDB or somewhere else)\n2. \"that prob wont start correctly till reboot\" - meaning the broken qdrant container won''t start until a reboot\n3. \"make sure that socket is right on qdrant advertsing the grpc port instead of http.. qdraqnt nativly supports grpc\"\n\nSo the user wants me to:\n- Check the qdrant configuration to make sure it''s using gRPC (port 6334) not HTTP (port 6333)\n- The cognitive-mcp already connects to `http://127.0.0.1:6334` which IS the gRPC port\n\nLet me check the qdrant_shuttle more carefully and also look at how qdrant was configured inside the container. But wait - the container is STOPPED and broken. The user says it won''t start until reboot.\n\nActually, let me re-read the user''s messages:\n- \"it isnt in pqdrant\" - qdrant isn''t in the qdrant container? Or the data isn''t there?\n- \"that prob wont start correctly till reboot\" - the broken qdrant container\n\nAnd the latest: \"make sure that socket is right on qdrant advertsing the grpc port instead of http.. qdraqnt nativly supports grpc\"\n\nI think they want me to make sure the cognitive-mcp code is using gRPC (port 6334) and not HTTP (port 6333). The code already uses6334 which is gRPC default.\n\nLet me look at the qdrant_shuttle.rs more carefully to understand the full picture, and check if there''s any HTTP reference.","time":{"start":1783671001091,"end":1783671005441}},"time":1783671005441}');
