INSERT INTO event VALUES('evt_f4b15eaf0001aupZaJYBvmekmo','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',2080,'message.part.updated.1','{"sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","part":{"id":"prt_f4b15d580001E4YpaXeBwljyrh","sessionID":"ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW","messageID":"msg_f4b15b54e00114PGDtnAJ3GeuR","type":"reasoning","text":"The `op-openvswitch-daemon` crate still has source files and is NOT in the workspace `Cargo.toml` members list. The CLAUDE.md says the daemon is deprecated. The files have some recent modifications (July 8).Wait, the user said \"op-openvswitch-daemon is deprecated\" and the notes say it''s already deleted from git commits `655d82a40` and `2022c3e94`. But the directory still exists with source files. Let me check if these are untracked or tracked.\n\nThe `git status crates/op-openvswitch-daemon/ --short` returned nothing, meaning these files are tracked and clean (not modified from HEAD). So the directory exists in the repo but isn''t in the workspace members.\n\nActually wait - looking at git status showing nothing, and the file dates showing Jul 3 and Jul 8 - these files are committed. Let me check if the directory was removed in those commits but then... hmm, the CLAUDE.md says these were deleted in the commits. But the directory still exists. Let me check what `git log` says.\n\nActually, let me re-read the summary more carefully:\n- \"DEPRECATED (now deleted from git): OvsdbDbusClient, rovs_proxy, op-openvswitch-daemon (daemon.rs, ovs.rs, main.rs, bin entry)\"\n- \"op-openvswitch-daemon: user confirms deprecated — already deleted from git in commits 655d82a40 and 2022c3e94\"\n\nBut the directory still has files and `git status` shows nothing - meaning these files are in HEAD. So maybe only daemon.rs, ovs.rs, and bin/main.rs were removed, not the whole crate. The CLAUDE.md notes say \"op-openvswitch-daemon is deprecated — don''t extend it.\"\n\nLet me check what was actually in those commits.","time":{"start":1783671149952,"end":1783671155440}},"time":1783671155440}');
