INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4afc19d4001ZCV4R1MkVYZpx6','msg_f4afbe643001bNEX43gya5gvhA','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783669463508,1783669469294,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user is asking about what we''ve done so far. Let me look at the previous summary and the current state. The user asked \"is the covsw controller declared as 10.200.0.1 on the bridge\" and then said \"Continue if you have next steps, or stop and ask for clarification if you are unsure how to proceed.\"\n\nFrom the investigation:\n- `ovsbr0` bridge has `10.200.0.1/30` and also `10.200.0.2/32` as secondary- CozoDB is listening on `10.200.0.1:8444`\n- gRPC bridge is listening on `10.200.0.1:50051`\n- DNS is on `10.200.0.1:53`\n- The CozoDB store is initialized (embedded, not over network) - the log says `op_cozo_store: CozoDB schema ready`\n- Qdrant is NOT running (failed to connect at `127.0.0.1:6334`)\n- Gemini fallback unavailable (no API key)\n- Identity sled not written (no WG_PUBKEY env var)\n\nThe user''s question \"is the covsw controller declared as 10.200.0.1 on the bridge\" - I think they''re asking about the CozoDB controller being on the bridge. The answer is yes - the CozoDB embedded database is at `/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db` (local), and the listening ports on `10.200.0.1` are for the gRPC bridge and the HTTP MCP endpoint.\n\nActually wait - \"covsw\" might be \"cozo-something\" or \"covsw\" as a specific term. Let me re-read. \"is the covsw controller declared as 10.200.0.1 on the bridge\" - maybe they mean the CozoDB? Or maybe it''s a typo for \"cozo\". Let me just answer what I found and continue with next steps.\n\nActually, looking more carefully - the user said \"is the covsw controller declared as 10.200.0.1 on the bridge\" - this might be asking about the CozoDB or maybe the \"covsw\" is something else. Let me just provide my findings and continue.\n\nLet me also check what''s listening on those ports and what the zeroclaw config says about the bridge.","time":{"start":1783669463508,"end":1783669469291}}');
