INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4afe09bf001nt0ikiGwh1WO7W','msg_f4afde510001HxUFlkcFJrYEV7','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783669590463,1783669598003,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"OK now I understand the architecture much better. The key insight from the user is:\n\n1. `OvsdbDbusClient` and `rovs_proxy` are deprecated - replaced by direct `rovs` commands via D-Bus\n2. `op-openvswitch-daemon` is deprecated\n3. `identity_sled.dat` is deprecated - the actual container IS the sled now\n\nLooking at the code:\n- `identity_sled_dispatch.rs` line 1: \"the container is the sled is the identity\" - this confirms the user''s point\n- The gRPC bridge''s `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` at line 1212 still takes `OvsdbDbusClient` - this is the deprecated path\n- The `rovs_commands` plugin is schema-only, the actual execution is in the gRPC bridge\n\nThe user is saying the new architecture is:\n- Direct `rovs` commands via D-Bus (not through `op-openvswitch-daemon`)\n- Container IS the sled (not a separate `identity_sled.dat` file)\n\nSo the `op-dbus-mirror` code that still references `OvsdbDbusClient` is deprecated dead code. The `op-grpc-bridge` mutation engine still dispatches through the deprecated `OvsdbDbusClient`.\n\nLet me understand what the user wants me to do next. They said \"Continue if you have next steps.\" The next steps from before were:\n1. Fix the port parsing bug in `grpc.rs:283`\n2. Fix `netmaker.rs` async/sync mismatch\n3. Run full workspace `cargo check`\n4. Investigate Qdrant\n5. Determine WG_PUBKEY for identity sled\n\nBut now with the new info that `OvsdbDbusClient` is deprecated, the port parsing bug in `grpc.rs` is in the deprecated path too. The user is telling me the architecture has changed.\n\nI should ask for clarification on what the current state is - is the `op-dbus-mirror` still used? Is the `op-grpc-bridge` the new path? What should I focus on?\n\nActually, the user said \"Continue if you have next steps, or stop and ask for clarification if you are unsure how to proceed.\" I think I should summarize what I''ve learned and ask for clarification on the current architecture, since several key components are deprecated.","time":{"start":1783669590463,"end":1783669598000}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4afe2735001aixGB7F7yqKBRp','msg_f4afde510001HxUFlkcFJrYEV7','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783669598005,1783669604155,'{"type":"text","text":"Good. Now I have a clear picture. Let me summarize the architectural state as I understand it:\n\n**Deprecated (dead code paths):**\n- `op-network/src/rovs_proxy.rs` — `OvsdbDbusClient`\n- `op-openvswitch-daemon` — entire crate\n- `op-dbus-mirror` — still imports `OvsdbDbusClient` in 3 files\n- `op-identity-sled` binary + `identity_sled.json` projection\n- `identity_sled.dat` / `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/identity_sled.json`\n\n**Current architecture:**\n- `rovs_commands` plugin (schema-only) → gRPC bridge `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` → direct `rovs` D-Bus calls\n- Container IS the sled — `identity_sled_dispatch.rs:1` confirms: \"the container is the sled is the identity\"\n- Sled state persists to Cozo (`identity_sleds` / `session_events` relations)\n- `provision_container` creates Incus instance + writes sled in one mutation\n\n**What I''m unsure about:**\n\n1. `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` at `mutation_engine.rs:1212` still takes `OvsdbDbusClient` — is this the deprecated path, or is it being actively migrated?\n2. `op-dbus-mirror` still references `OvsdbDbusClient` — is this crate fully deprecated or still in use?\n3. Is the port visibility issue (`list_ports` not showing ports) still relevant, or does the new `rovs` direct path handle this differently?","time":{"start":1783669598005,"end":1783669604153}}');
