INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b0c54b4001UbiVvPZHbdrk9k','msg_f4b0c39ed001pF3yiKhxs32dG7','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783670527157,1783670530873,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"OK so let me understand:\n\n1. **qdrant** - failed to start because of missing btrfs storage path: `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/rootfs`. This is a storage issue from when btrfs was restructured.\n\n2. **xray config** - the broken symlink points to `/dev/shm/xray-ghostbridge.json` which was being generated by the inference model. The backup `config.json.bak-20260707200129` has a real, working config with:\n   - NextDNS: `https://dns.nextdns.io/689ec7/Ghostbridge-Incus`\n   - TLS inbound on 443 (vless)\n   - Reality inbound on 8443 (vless + xtls-rprx-vision)\n   - Reality private key: `sEMA483j7RnPhQTqTcoqw5NUfuQ8TF12jc6yph_hhmc`\n\n3. The user mentions \"xray ridge header with nixtdns\" - they''re talking about the xray config having the Reality inbound (\"ridge\" = Reality) with NextDNS (\"nixtdns\") in the DNS section. They''re saying they''re not sure how it happened.\n\nSo the user is asking about:\n1. Making sure qdrant auto-starts in incus (not s6) - qdrant container is broken due to btrfs storage issue\n2. Understanding/fixing the xray config situation - the symlink is broken, needs to be a real file or the backup needs to be restored\n\nLet me address the qdrant storage issue and the xray config.","time":{"start":1783670527157,"end":1783670530846}}');
