INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b18c3a50012LyX1c7YHMmtO0','msg_f4b18b5f5001wPviZgbtlsUvqE','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783671341989,1783671343941,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"Let me analyze the conversation history and the previous summary to create an updated summary.\n\nKey new information from the conversation:\n1. User asked about qdrant - \"i hope the qdrant isnt gone i spent alot of time and $ vectorizing\"\n2. I tried to investigate but the command was user-aborted\n3. User asked \"did you do btrfs subvolume list /\" - suggesting they want me to run `btrfs subvolume list /` to check all subvolumes on the system, not just in the btrfs-pool directory\n\nThe user seems to think that the qdrant data might still exist somewhere as a btrfs subvolume, and wants me to check the root filesystem''s subvolumes. Let me update the summary with this new context.","time":{"start":1783671341989,"end":1783671343938}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b18cb48001VdewmkeQBHjUYS','msg_f4b18b5f5001wPviZgbtlsUvqE','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783671343944,1783671381158,'{"type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Fix compilation errors/warnings across the operation-dbus-proto Rust workspace, audit all D-Bus interfaces for correctness, diagnose why OVS ports visible via `ip a` are not returned by OVS D-Bus commands, and assess cognitive MCP system integration.\n- Ensure `gemma` and `ollama` s6 services do not start at boot (inference agent replaced by routing plugin).\n- Ensure a minimal xray config is available even when the inference model is down.\n- Ensure qdrant auto-starts in Incus, not as an s6 service on the host.\n- Verify netclient autostart as systemd daemon inside Incus containers (with uix socket modification).\n- **Recover qdrant vector data** — user spent significant time and money vectorizing; data may still exist as a btrfs subvolume on the root filesystem (`btrfs subvolume list /` not yet run).\n\n## Important Details\n- Workspace root: `/home/jeremy/git/operation-dbus-proto`\n- **Branch**: `working-tree-clean` (detached HEAD at `655d82a40`)\n- **Latest commits**: `2022c3e94 op-grpc-bridge: remove deprecated OVS paths`, `655d82a40 op-openvswitch-daemon: remove deprecated daemon`\n- **DEPRECATED (now deleted from git)**: `OvsdbDbusClient`, `rovs_proxy`, `op-openvswitch-daemon` (daemon.rs, ovs.rs, main.rs, bin entry), `op-dbus-mirror` event dead code — all replaced by direct `rovs` commands via D-Bus or `StateEngine` plugin calls\n- **`OvsdbDbusClient` completely removed** — `mutation_engine.rs:dispatch_rovs_commands_method` now calls `StateEngine::get().method_call(\"rovs_commands\", ...)` directly\n- **`OvsdbClient` trait** still exists in `op-openvswitch-daemon` crate (deprecated/dead) — no live callers remain\n- **No more `rovs_proxy.rs`** — deleted in latest commits\n- **NEW ARCHITECTURE**: Container IS the sled (no separate identity sled binary/file); `rovs_commands` plugin has a **sealed blob** (`rovs_commands.e359cd0c2cc3b1eb.blob`) backed by its schema\n- **OVS port visibility issue**: ports show on bridge via `ip a show` but not via OVS D-Bus commands\n- **Identity sled projection**: `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/identity_sled.json` exists but is **empty** — `{\"sleds\":[]}`, no sleds registered\n- **op-cognitive-mcp**: running (PID 739, up ~5326s), HTTP on `0.0.0.0:3003`, gRPC on `0.0.0.0:50052`, CozoDB embedded at `/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db`\n- **Qdrant**: NOT running — no process, no port 6334; \"Qdrant Semantic Shuttle unavailable\"\n- **Identity sled**: NOT written — log warns: \"Could not read WireGuard public key — identity sled not written; set WG_PUBKEY env var to override\"\n- **Gemini fallback**: unavailable — no `GEMINI_API_KEY` or `COGNITIVE_MCP_GEMINI_API_KEY` set\n- **ovsbr0 bridge**: `10.200.0.1/30` (primary), `10.0.0.2/32` (secondary), `10.200.0.2/32` (secondary) — CozoDB on `10.200.0.1:8444`, gRPC bridge on `10.200.0.1:50051`, DNS on `10.200.0.1:53`\n- **S6 gemma/ollama already disabled at boot**: all three services (`gemma`, `ollama`, `ollama-srv`) have `down` files in `/etc/s6/sv/` — confirmed present ✅\n- **gbr-xray**: s6 longrun, depends on `gemma` and `gbr-warp` (via `dependencies.d/`); run script exits cleanly (exit 0) if `/etc/xray/config.json` is missing\n- **gbr-xray config**: **FIXED** ✅ — restored from backup via `sudo cp /etc/xray/config.json.bak-20260707200129 /etc/xray/config.json` (5872 bytes)\n- **Last working xray backup**: `config.json.bak-20260707200129` — contains NextDNS (`dns.nextdns.io/689ec7/Ghostbridge-Incus`), Reality inbound on 8443 (private key `sEMA483j7RnPhQTqTcoqw5NUfuQ8TF12jc6yph_hhmc`), TLS inbound on 443\n- **op-openvswitch-daemon**: user confirms deprecated — already deleted from git in commits `655d82a40` and `2022c3e94`\n- **Incus storage pools**: `array` (btrfs), `btrfs-pool` (btrfs, source: `/opt/incus/storage-pool`), `default` (btrfs), `netmaker-pool` (btrfs); backing device `/dev/sda3` (486GB, 93% used, 39GB free)\n- **btrfs-pool mount**: `/dev/sda3 on /var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool type btrfs` (subvolid=331, subvol=`/@/opt/incus/storage-pool`) — **mounted and accessible** ✅\n- **Default incus profile**: uses `btrfs-pool` for root disk device; 9 instances reference it\n- **btrfs-pool contents**: 444.59GiB used of 486.00GiB; btrfs subvolume list of btrfs-pool shows only 3 UUID-named containers (`4991a337`, `578a6e31`, `9431b9db`) — **qdrant subvolume missing**\n- **qdrant container**: subvolume genuinely gone from btrfs-pool; Incus metadata references it but no btrfs subvolume exists; created `2026/07/08 13:24`, `boot.autostart: \"true\"`, `boot.autostart.priority: \"10\"`, Ubuntu jammy amd64, device `ghostbridge-socket` mounts `/run/ghostbridge`\n- **Architecture**: Each container''s namespace memory is a btrfs storage device tracked in **CozoDB**, added to blob btrfs root filesystem via `btrfs device add` for persistence\n- **Blob filesystem**: `/dev/shm/opdbus/plugin-blobs/` (on tmpfs) contains sealed plugin blobs (`.blob` files) with embedded JSON schemas; referenced plugins: btrfs, incus, cozo, cognitive_mcp, etc.\n- **netclient in Incus**: **running inside `netmaker-pro`** container — `/usr/local/bin/netclient daemon` (PID 803), `systemctl is-enabled netclient` → `enabled` ✅; user mentions UIX socket modification\n- **Incus container states**: `9431b9db` RUNNING (no IP), `netmaker-pro` RUNNING (100.90.37.1), `test-launch` RUNNING (no IP), all others STOPPED\n- **xray s6 services**: `s6-supervise op-xray-daemon` (PID 357) and `s6-supervise xray` (PID 426) running; config now restored\n- **qdrant gRPC**: cognitive-mcp''s `QdrantSemanticShuttle` connects to `http://127.0.0.1:6334` (gRPC) via `qdrant_client::Qdrant::from_url()`; qdrant natively supports gRPC on port 6334\n- **qdrant container broken state**: `btrfs subvolume show` fails (\"Not a Btrfs subvolume: Invalid argument\"); `incus delete qdrant --force` fails; only `backup.yaml` (2937 bytes) was in `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/` — dir now removed\n- **Incus storage volume `qdrant`**: still registered in incus storage DB as container volume on btrfs-pool; cannot delete via API (\"volumes of type container cannot be deleted with the storage API\")\n- **User''s qdrant concern**: user spent \"a lot of time and $ vectorizing\" — data preservation is critical; `btrfs subvolume list /` (root-level) has NOT been run yet — qdrant data may exist as a subvolume on the root filesystem or `/dev/sda3` that wasn''t checked\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Deleted `gemma_brain.rs` (384 lines) — replaced by routing plugin; cleaned `mod.rs` and `plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs`\n- Deleted `OvsdbDbusClient` and `OvsdbDbusClientInner` from `mutation_engine.rs` (~140 lines) — now calls `StateEngine::get().method_call(\"rovs_commands\", ...)`\n- Deleted `rovs_proxy.rs` — no longer needed\n- Deleted `op-openvswitch-daemon` daemon/ovs/bin/main source files (staged in `655d82a40`)\n- Added `routing.rs`, `routing_dispatch.rs`, `routing_plugin_schema` re-export\n- Added routing dispatch in `mutation_engine.rs` (mutate path + dispatch switch)\n- Fixed `jsonrpc_interface.rs`: removed dead code (57 lines orphaned struct/impl)\n- Fixed `event_dispatcher.rs:152`: removed stale `MirrorEvent::NonNet` match arm\n- Fixed `host_identity.rs:11`, `registration.rs:9`, `op-identity-sled.rs:3`: removed unused imports\n- `cargo check -p op-dbus-mirror` and `-p op-identity` verified clean\n- Confirmed all uncommitted diffs via `git diff HEAD` — changes consistent with refactor\n- Deleted all deprecated OVS paths from `op-grpc-bridge/src/lib.rs` (imports, trait impl, re-exports)\n- Cleaned up `main.rs` to remove daemon references\n- Confirmed `gemma`, `ollama`, `ollama-srv` s6 services all have `down` files — already disabled at boot ✅\n- Set qdrant incus `boot.autostart: \"true\"` and `boot.autostart.priority: \"10\"` ✅\n- Confirmed netclient running as systemd daemon inside `netmaker-pro` Incus container (enabled, PID 803)\n- Confirmed btrfs-pool is mounted and accessible at `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/`\n- Confirmed qdrant container rootfs subvolume is missing from btrfs-pool (only 3 UUID-named containers in btrfs subvolume list)\n- **Restored xray config** ✅ — `sudo rm /etc/xray/config.json && sudo cp ...bak-20260707200129 /etc/xray/config.json` (5872 bytes)\n- Confirmed xray s6 supervisors running (op-xray-daemon PID 357, xray PID 426)\n- Confirmed netclient running inside `netmaker-pro` as systemd daemon with UIX socket\n- Confirmed cognitive-mcp `QdrantSemanticShuttle` already uses gRPC port 6334 (not HTTP 6333) ✅\n- Investigated qdrant container failure: subvolume corrupted, only `backup.yaml` remains, `btrfs subvolume show` fails, `incus delete` fails — rootfs subvolume genuinely lost\n- Removed `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/` directory\n- Attempted `incus storage volume delete btrfs-pool container/qdrant` — failed (\"volumes of type container cannot be deleted with storage API\")\n- Attempted `incus launch images:ubuntu/jammy/amd64 qdrant` — failed (\"Instance qdrant already exists\") — incus metadata still references old instance\n\n### Active\n- **Recovering qdrant vector data**: need to run `sudo btrfs subvolume list /` to find any qdrant-related subvolumes on root filesystem or `/dev/sda3` that may contain the vectorized data\n- Uncommitted changes: `op-grpc-bridge/src/lib.rs`, `main.rs`, `mutation_engine.rs`, plus cognitive-mcp changes and deploy script updates\n- Untracked files: `identity_source.rs`, `down`, `zeroclaw-routing-uigen/` directory\n- Diagnosing OVS D-Bus `list_ports` not showing ports visible via `ip a show`\n- Assessing cognitive MCP integration — CozoDB and gRPC functional, Qdrant and Gemini fallback unavailable\n- Identity sled investigation: not running, needs `WG_PUBKEY` env var, projection empty\n- Ensuring `gbr-xray` works without gemma dependency (gemma replaced by routing plugin)\n- Understanding how xray config ended up with Reality + NextDNS combination\n\n### Blocked\n- **qdrant incus won''t start/recreate**: btrfs container subvolume missing and incus metadata still references old instance; `incus delete --force` fails (\"Not a Btrfs subvolume: Invalid argument\"); plain dir removed but incus still thinks instance exists; may need reboot to clear incus state; user confirms \"that probably won''t start correctly till reboot\"\n- **qdrant vector data recovery**: user invested significant time and money in vectorizing; `btrfs subvolume list /` on root not yet run — data may exist elsewhere on disk\n- `op-plugins/src/state_plugins/netmaker.rs:317`: async/sync mismatch — `get_node()` calls `.await` but trait `StatePlugin` method is synchronous\n- Identity sled not running — needs `WG_PUBKEY` env var to generate identity; projection remains empty\n- Gemini API key not configured — fallback unavailable\n- Full workspace `cargo check` attempted but timed out (180s)\n- Deprecated `op-openvswitch-daemon` crate still exists in Cargo.toml workspace members (source files deleted but crate shell remains)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Run `sudo btrfs subvolume list /` on the root filesystem to find any qdrant-related subvolumes containing vector data\n2. Remove `gemma` from `gbr-xray/dependencies.d/` — gemma replaced by routing plugin\n3. Remove `op-openvswitch-daemon` from workspace `Cargo.toml` members list\n4. Commit all remaining uncommitted changes (`lib.rs`, `main.rs`, `mutation_engine.rs` cleanup, cognitive-mcp updates, deploy scripts)\n5. Fix `netmaker.rs` async/sync mismatch\n6. Determine what `WG_PUBKEY` to set for identity sled generation\n7. Verify netclient uix socket modification in `netmaker-pro`\n8. Reboot to clear stuck incus qdrant metadata, then recreate qdrant container on btrfs-pool with gRPC port 6334 confirmed\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/mutation_engine.rs`: `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` — now uses `StateEngine::method_call(\"rovs_commands\", ...)` directly\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/lib.rs`: uncommitted — removed deprecated OVS imports, trait impl, re-exports\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/main.rs`: uncommitted — cleaned daemon references\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/routing_dispatch.rs`: routing dispatch (new)\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/routing.rs`: routing plugin (new)\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/gemma_brain.rs`: **deleted** — fully removed, no references remain\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/mod.rs`: removed `gemma_brain`, added `routing`\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs`: removed `gemma_brain_schema`, added `routing_schema`\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/cognitive_mcp.rs`: collection name `repomix_rag` → `repos_lsp_rust_voyage_4_large`\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/incus.rs`: retry on empty container name\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/large_language_model.rs`: removed brand-brain fallback\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/netmaker.rs`: async/sync mismatch bug\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/identity_source.rs`: **new** (untracked) — container identity resolution\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/interceptor.rs`: expanded with identity_source integration\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/qdrant_shuttle.rs`: added `find_collection` helper; DEFAULT_QDRANT_URL = `http://127.0.0.1:6334` (gRPC)\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/rag_pipeline.rs`: `list_collections` failure now non-fatal\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/Cargo.toml`: added `base64` dependency\n- `crates/op-web/src/wireguard.rs`: removed manual `config_check` D-Bus method, added `generate_client_config_with_psk`\n- `docs/routing-plugin-spec.md`: routing plugin spec (new)\n- `deploy/s6/gemma/run`: now uses `zcall routing derive/publish` with fallback\n- `deploy/s6/gemma/shell_up`: same zcall routing pattern\n- `deploy/s6/gemma/down`: **new** — `zcall routing uninvoke` + cache state\n- `deploy/s6/zeroclaw-routing-uigen/`: **new** deploy directory\n- `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/run`: xray REALITY egress; exits cleanly if config missing; sources xray.env\n- `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/dependencies.d/gemma`: **needs removal** — gemma replaced by routing\n- `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/dependencies.d/gbr-warp`: xray depends on gbr-warp\n- `/etc/s6/sv/gemma/down`: exists — gemma disabled at boot ✅\n- `/etc/s6/sv/ollama/down`: exists — ollama disabled at boot ✅\n- `/etc/s6/sv/ollama-srv/down`: exists — ollama-srv disabled at boot ✅\n- `/etc/xray/config.json`: **FIXED** ✅ — restored from backup (5872 bytes)\n- `/etc/xray/config.json.bak-20260707200129`: last working backup with Reality + NextDNS config\n- `/etc/xray/tls.crt`, `/etc/xray/tls.key`: TLS certs present\n- `/etc/ghostbridge/xray.env`: xray environment sourced by gbr-xray\n- `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/identity_sled.json`: **empty** `{\"sleds\":[]}`\n- `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/zeroclaw`: (referenced in blob system)\n- `/etc/s6/sv/op-cognitive-mcp/run`: env `COGNITIVE_MCP_DB_PATH=/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db`, `WG_INTERFACE=netmaker`\n- `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/`: **deleted** (was only `backup.yaml`)\n- `/dev/sda3`: 486GB btrfs device backing btrfs-pool, 93% used, 39GB free","time":{"start":1783671343944,"end":1783671381153}}');
