INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b293f8e001XqEGoL4Ki9FZxl','msg_f4b292b74001x4rxqtm93JdSXt','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783672422287,1783672422291,'{"snapshot":"dbf21a1ec73382190729d4cfc1bf71f3395b2de3","type":"step-start"}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b293f970014VbQjv4lT2bDlc','msg_f4b292b74001x4rxqtm93JdSXt','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783672422295,1783672426781,'{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user is asking me to recall what we were discussing before the disk cleanup tangent. Let me look at the conversation summary.\n\nFrom the context:\n\n1. The user asked \"What did we do so far?\" - which triggered the detailed summary to be shown\n2. Then the user asked \"did you do btrfs subvolume list /\" \n3. I ran `sudo btrfs subvolume list /` - found no qdrant subvolume anywhere\n4. I reported the bad news - qdrant vector data is gone from btrfs\n5. But noted CozoDB database at `/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db` has its own copy of the indexed data\n\n\n6. Then the conversation shifted to disk cleanup when the user asked to check disk usage and delete build artifacts since btrfs fills up easily, so we removed the target/ directory and other cache files\n\nBefore all that, we were trying to recover the user''s qdrant vector data - they''d invested significant time and money in vectorizing, and I was looking for any qdrant-related subvolumes on the root filesystem. The investigation turned up empty, but I''d pointed out that CozoDB might still have the indexed data even though the qdrant subvolume was gone.\n\nThe real issue is that the `QdrantSemanticShuttle` component is trying to connect to qdrant at `http://127.0.0.1:6334`, but qdrant isn''t actually running - no process, no port listening. So even though CozoDB has the data, the system can''t access it because the service isn''t up.","time":{"start":1783672422295,"end":1783672426779}}');
INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b295120001MAjY9gHgFDoVPm','msg_f4b292b74001x4rxqtm93JdSXt','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783672426784,1783672429096,'{"type":"text","text":"We were investigating **qdrant vector data recovery**. You said you spent a lot of time and money vectorizing, and we were checking if the data survived.\n\nWhat I found:\n- **No qdrant subvolume exists** anywhere in the btrfs tree (checked all 40 subvolumes on root)\n- **No qdrant container** in btrfs-pool — only 3 Incus container subvolumes (`4991a337`, `578a6e31`, `9431b9db`) — none are qdrant\n- qdrant was **not running** (no process, no port 6334 listening)\n- The cognitive-mcp `QdrantSemanticShuttle` reports \"unavailable\"\n\nI suggested checking **CozoDB** (`/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db`) because the `RagPipeline` has its own copy of indexed data in the `repos_lsp_rust_voyage_4_large` collection — that might have survived even if qdrant didn''t. Want me to check what''s in CozoDB?","time":{"start":1783672426784,"end":1783672429094}}');
