INSERT INTO part VALUES('prt_f4b3288dc001ZKUMKJ6cQU9hvg','msg_f4b32811d001fKD0VAIih092FA','ses_0b516ef36ffeY2Uc26WsdLIdZW',1783673030876,1783673082301,'{"type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Fix compilation errors/warnings across the operation-dbus-proto Rust workspace, audit all D-Bus interfaces for correctness, diagnose why OVS ports visible via `ip a` are not returned by OVS D-Bus commands, and assess cognitive MCP system integration.\n- Ensure `gemma` and `ollama` s6 services do not start at boot (inference agent replaced by routing plugin).\n- Ensure a minimal xray config is available even when the inference model is down.\n- Ensure qdrant auto-starts in Incus, not as an s6 service on the host.\n- Verify netclient autostart as systemd daemon inside Incus containers (with uix socket modification).\n- Recover qdrant vector data — user spent significant time and money vectorizing.\n- **Clean up disk usage** — btrfs root was 93% full; cleaned to 67%.\n- **Find qdrant rootfs in Incus storage pool** — user asked to look in btrfs-pool for the container rootfs.\n\n## Important Details\n- Workspace root: `/home/jeremy/git/operation-dbus-proto`\n- **Branch**: `working-tree-clean` (detached HEAD at `655d82a40`)\n- **Latest commits**: `2022c3e94 op-grpc-bridge: remove deprecated OVS paths`, `655d82a40 op-openvswitch-daemon: remove deprecated daemon`\n- **DEPRECATED (now deleted from git)**: `OvsdbDbusClient`, `rovs_proxy`, `op-openvswitch-daemon` (daemon.rs, ovs.rs, main.rs, bin entry), `op-dbus-mirror` event dead code — all replaced by direct `rovs` commands via D-Bus or `StateEngine` plugin calls\n- **`OvsdbDbusClient` completely removed** — `mutation_engine.rs:dispatch_rovs_commands_method` now calls `StateEngine::get().method_call(\"rovs_commands\", ...)` directly\n- **`OvsdbClient` trait** still exists in `op-openvswitch-daemon` crate (deprecated/dead) — no live callers remain\n- **No more `rovs_proxy.rs`** — deleted in latest commits\n- **NEW ARCHITECTURE**: Container IS the sled (no separate identity sled binary/file); `rovs_commands` plugin has a **sealed blob** (`rovs_commands.e359cd0c2cc3b1eb.blob`) backed by its schema\n- **OVS port visibility issue**: ports show on bridge via `ip a show` but not via OVS D-Bus commands\n- **Identity sled projection**: `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/identity_sled.json` exists but is **empty** — `{\"sleds\":[]}`, no sleds registered\n- **op-cognitive-mcp**: running (HTTP `0.0.0.0:3003`, gRPC `0.0.0.0:50052`), CozoDB at `/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db` — health OK ✅\n- **CozoDB**: only **520K** on disk — essentially empty; `blobs/` directory empty; not a source of recovered vector data\n- **Qdrant data FOUND** ✅: `/var/lib/qdrant` exists with **28GB** of vectorized data on host root filesystem\n- **Qdrant collections** (at `/var/lib/qdrant/storage/collections/`):\n  - `repos_lsp_rust_voyage_4_large` — **4.8G**\n  - `rust_lang_rust_lsp_voyage_code_3` — **3.2G**\n  - `repos_lsp_go_voyage_4_large` — **1.5G**\n  - `repos_specs_docs_voyage_4_lite` — **666M**\n  - `repos_lsp_c_cpp_voyage_4_lite` — **411M**\n  - `repos_lsp_go_voyage_4_lite` — **369M**\n  - `repos_lsp_python_voyage_4_large` — **347M**\n  - `repos_lsp_java_voyage_4_lite` — **246M**\n  - `repos_lsp_python_voyage_4_lite` — **193M**\n  - `repos_lsp_typescript_voyage_4_lite` — **104M**\n  - `rust_lang_rust_voyage_code_3` — **25M**\n- **Qdrant backups**: `/var/lib/qdrant.bak-20260529-203749` (4.5G), `/var/lib/qdrant-rescue` (4.5G)\n- **Qdrant snapshots** found at: `/.snapshots/root-20260611-000320/var/lib/qdrant`, `/.snapshots/zeroclaw/var/lib/qdrant`, `/.snapshots/@blob-base/var/lib/qdrant`\n- **Qdrant is NOT currently running** — no process, no port 6334; \"Qdrant Semantic Shuttle unavailable\"\n- **Qdrant incus container broken**: subvolume corrupted, btrfs subvolume show fails, incus delete fails, metadata still references old instance\n- **Qdrant gRPC**: cognitive-mcp connects to `http://127.0.0.1:6334` (gRPC)\n- **qdrant NOT found in btrfs-pool storage**: `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/` was deleted (only contained `backup.yaml`); no qdrant btrfs subvolume exists in the storage pool''s subvolume list; incus metadata referencing old instance exists in `storage-pools-volumes/` and `containers-snapshots/` but no actual rootfs\n- **Identity sled**: NOT running, needs `WG_PUBKEY` env var; projection empty\n- **Gemini fallback**: unavailable — no API key set\n- **ovsbr0 bridge**: `10.200.0.1/30` (primary), `10.0.0.2/32` (secondary), `10.200.0.2/32` (secondary)\n- **S6 gemma/ollama already disabled at boot**: all three services have `down` files ✅\n- **gbr-xray**: s6 longrun, depends on `gemma` and `gbr-warp`; run script exits cleanly if config missing\n- **gbr-xray config**: **FIXED** ✅ — restored from backup (5872 bytes)\n- **Last working xray backup**: `config.json.bak-20260707200129`\n- **op-openvswitch-daemon**: confirmed deprecated — deleted from git in commits `655d82a40` and `2022c3e94`\n- **Disk usage**: `/dev/sda3` 486GB; **cleaned to 67%** (320G used, 163G free) from 93%\n- **Disk cleanup performed**: `target/` (211G), `~/.cache/paru` (18G), `~/.cache/JetBrains` (13G), `~/.npm` (2.3G), `~/.cache/go-build` (1.5G), `~/.cache/pip` (214M), `pacman -Scc`\n- **Remaining cleanable caches**: `~/.cache/uv` (3.3G), `~/.cache/google-chrome` (1.4G), `~/.cache/ms-playwright` (646M)\n- **Incus storage pools**: `array` (btrfs), `btrfs-pool` (btrfs, source: `/opt/incus/storage-pool`), `default` (btrfs on loop0), `netmaker-pool` (btrfs)\n- **btrfs-pool mount**: `/dev/sda3 on /var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool type btrfs` (subvolid=331, subvol=`/@/opt/incus/storage-pool`) ✅\n- **Default incus profile**: uses `btrfs-pool` for root disk device; 9 instances reference it\n- **btrfs-pool contents**: 444.59GiB used of 486.00GiB; btrfs subvolume list shows only 3 UUID-named containers (`4991a337`, `578a6e31`, `9431b9db`) — **no qdrant subvolume**\n- **btrfs-pool container dirs**: `4991a337/`, `578a6e31/`, `9431b9db/`, `containers-snapshots/`, `custom-udev/`, `images/`, `isos/`, `networks/`, `projects/`, `storage-pools-volumes/`, `virtual-machines/` — **no qdrant**\n- **Root btrfs subvolumes**: 40 total — includes `@`, `@home`, `@log`, `@pkg`, `@snapshots`, `@backup`, `@bridge`, `@part`, blockchain vectors, Incus array images, `@blob-zeroclaw-*`, `@blob-ghostbridge-socket`\n- **Architecture**: Each container''s namespace memory is a btrfs storage device tracked in **CozoDB**, added to blob btrfs root filesystem via `btrfs device add`\n- **Blob filesystem**: `/dev/shm/opdbus/plugin-blobs/` (on tmpfs)\n- **netclient in Incus**: running inside `netmaker-pro` — `/usr/local/bin/netclient daemon` (PID 803), `systemctl is-enabled netclient` → `enabled` ✅\n- **Incus container states**: `9431b9db` RUNNING (no IP), `netmaker-pro` RUNNING (100.90.37.1), `test-launch` RUNNING (no IP), all others STOPPED\n- **xray s6 services**: `s6-supervise op-xray-daemon` (PID 357) and `s6-supervise xray` (PID 426) running\n- **Incus storage volume `qdrant`**: still registered in incus storage DB as container volume on btrfs-pool; cannot delete via API (\"volumes of type container cannot be deleted with the storage API\")\n- **op-cognitive-mcp s6 service**: `/etc/s6/sv/op-cognitive-mcp/run` — depends only on `dbus-session`; env: `COGNITIVE_MCP_DB_PATH=/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db`, `WG_INTERFACE=netmaker`\n- **Qdrant s6 service (HOST)**: created at `/etc/s6/sv/qdrant/` with config at `/etc/qdrant/config.yaml`; points to `/var/lib/qdrant/storage`; hosts gRPC on `127.0.0.1:6334`, HTTP on `127.0.0.1:6333`\n- **Qdrant s6 service NOT starting**: `s6-svc` returns \"supervisor not listening\" — s6-svscan runs under `/run/service/` but doesn''t pick up `/etc/s6/sv/qdrant/` (needs to be in `/run/service/` or registered via s6-rc)\n- **s6 supervision model**: PID 1 is `s6-svscan -X3 -- /run/service`; services must be linked/copied into `/run/service/` to be supervised\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Deleted `gemma_brain.rs` (384 lines) — replaced by routing plugin; cleaned `mod.rs` and `plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs`\n- Deleted `OvsdbDbusClient` and `OvsdbDbusClientInner` from `mutation_engine.rs` (~140 lines) — now calls `StateEngine::get().method_call(\"rovs_commands\", ...)`\n- Deleted `rovs_proxy.rs` — no longer needed\n- Deleted `op-openvswitch-daemon` daemon/ovs/bin/main source files (staged in `655d82a40`)\n- Added `routing.rs`, `routing_dispatch.rs`, `routing_plugin_schema` re-export\n- Added routing dispatch in `mutation_engine.rs` (mutate path + dispatch switch)\n- Fixed `jsonrpc_interface.rs`: removed dead code (57 lines orphaned struct/impl)\n- Fixed `event_dispatcher.rs:152`: removed stale `MirrorEvent::NonNet` match arm\n- Fixed `host_identity.rs:11`, `registration.rs:9`, `op-identity-sled.rs:3`: removed unused imports\n- `cargo check -p op-dbus-mirror` and `-p op-identity` verified clean\n- Deleted all deprecated OVS paths from `op-grpc-bridge/src/lib.rs` (imports, trait impl, re-exports)\n- Cleaned up `main.rs` to remove daemon references\n- Confirmed `gemma`, `ollama`, `ollama-srv` s6 services all have `down` files — already disabled at boot ✅\n- Set qdrant incus `boot.autostart: \"true\"` and `boot.autostart.priority: \"10\"` ✅\n- Confirmed netclient running as systemd daemon inside `netmaker-pro` Incus container (enabled, PID 803)\n- Confirmed btrfs-pool is mounted and accessible at `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/`\n- Confirmed qdrant container rootfs subvolume is missing from btrfs-pool\n- **Restored xray config** ✅ — `sudo cp ...bak-20260707200129 /etc/xray/config.json` (5872 bytes)\n- Confirmed xray s6 supervisors running (op-xray-daemon PID 357, xray PID 426)\n- Confirmed cognitive-mcp `QdrantSemanticShuttle` already uses gRPC port 6334 ✅\n- Investigated qdrant container failure: subvolume corrupted, only `backup.yaml` remains\n- Removed `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers/qdrant/` directory\n- **Disk cleanup executed**: `target/` (211G), `~/.cache/paru` (18G), `~/.cache/JetBrains` (13G), `~/.npm` (2.3G), `~/.cache/go-build` (1.5G), `~/.cache/pip` (214M), `pacman -Scc` — total ~247G freed; root **93% → 67%** ✅\n- CozoDB checked: only 520K, empty — no vectorized data in CozoDB\n- **Discovered qdrant vector data EXISTS** ✅: `/var/lib/qdrant` = **28G** on root filesystem with 11 collections; `.bak` copies (4.5G each) and btrfs snapshots also found\n- User corrected earlier assessment — data is on the root filesystem (home subvolume), was never lost\n- **Searched btrfs-pool for qdrant rootfs**: confirmed NOT present — no `containers/qdrant/` dir, no qdrant subvolume in btrfs pool subvolume list, no qdrant entry in `storage-pools-volumes/`; only 3 actual container subvolumes exist (`4991a337`, `578a6e31`, `9431b9db`)\n- **Created host s6 qdrant service**: config at `/etc/qdrant/config.yaml`, run script at `/etc/s6/sv/qdrant/run` (execlineb, runs `qdrant --config-path /etc/qdrant/config.yaml`)\n- **Verified qdrant binary**: `/usr/local/bin/qdrant` — v1.18.2, statically linked (pie), exists and executable\n- **s6-svc failed**: \"unable to control /etc/s6/sv/qdrant: supervisor not listening\" — services must be in `/run/service/` to be supervised by s6-svscan\n\n### Active\n- Uncommitted changes: `op-grpc-bridge/src/lib.rs`, `main.rs`, `mutation_engine.rs`, plus cognitive-mcp changes and deploy script updates\n- Untracked files: `identity_source.rs`, `down`, `zeroclaw-routing-uigen/` directory\n- Diagnosing OVS D-Bus `list_ports` not showing ports visible via `ip a show`\n- Assessing cognitive MCP integration — CozoDB and gRPC functional, Qdrant and Gemini fallback unavailable\n- Identity sled investigation: not running, needs `WG_PUBKEY` env var; projection empty\n- Ensuring `gbr-xray` works without gemma dependency (gemma replaced by routing plugin)\n- **Getting qdrant running on host**: s6 service created but not supervised; need to either link into `/run/service/`, use s6-rc, or start qdrant directly\n- **Next**: Start qdrant process pointing at `/var/lib/qdrant` data so cognitive-mcp can use it\n\n### Blocked\n- **qdrant incus won''t start/recreate**: btrfs container subvolume missing and incus metadata still references old instance; `incus delete --force` fails; may need reboot to clear incus state\n- **qdrant s6 service not supervised**: s6-svscan runs at `/run/service/` but `/etc/s6/sv/qdrant/` is not linked; need to determine correct registration method\n- `op-plugins/src/state_plugins/netmaker.rs:317`: async/sync mismatch — `get_node()` calls `.await` but trait `StatePlugin` method is synchronous\n- Identity sled not running — needs `WG_PUBKEY` env var to generate identity; projection remains empty\n- Gemini API key not configured — fallback unavailable\n- Full workspace `cargo check` attempted but timed out (180s)\n- Deprecated `op-openvswitch-daemon` crate still exists in Cargo.toml workspace members (source files deleted but crate shell remains)\n\n## Next Move\n1. **Start qdrant process directly** — run `qdrant --config-path /etc/qdrant/config.yaml` in background (or `exec` from a supervised context) to get it serving on `127.0.0.1:6334` immediately, bypassing s6 registration issue\n2. **Verify cognitive-mcp can reach qdrant** — after qdrant is up, confirm `QdrantSemanticShuttle` connects successfully\n3. **Commit all uncommitted changes** — `lib.rs`, `main.rs`, `mutation_engine.rs` cleanup, cognitive-mcp updates, deploy scripts\n4. Remove `gemma` from `gbr-xray/dependencies.d/` — gemma replaced by routing plugin\n5. Remove `op-openvswitch-daemon` from workspace `Cargo.toml` members list\n6. Fix `netmaker.rs` async/sync mismatch\n7. Determine what `WG_PUBKEY` to set for identity sled generation\n8. Verify netclient uix socket modification in `netmaker-pro`\n9. Clean up stuck incus qdrant metadata after reboot\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/var/lib/qdrant/`: **28G vector data** — 11 collections with Voyage embeddings (rust, go, python, java, typescript, c/c++, specs/docs)\n- `/var/lib/qdrant/storage/collections/`: all collection dirs with `segments/`, `config.json`, etc.\n- `/var/lib/qdrant.bak-20260529-203749/`: 4.5G backup of qdrant data\n- `/var/lib/qdrant-rescue/`: 4.5G rescue copy\n- `/.snapshots/root-20260611-000320/var/lib/qdrant/`: btrfs snapshot of qdrant data\n- `/.snapshots/zeroclaw/var/lib/qdrant/`: btrfs snapshot\n- `/.snapshots/@blob-base/var/lib/qdrant/`: btrfs snapshot\n- `/usr/local/bin/qdrant`: qdrant binary v1.18.2, static pie linked\n- `/etc/qdrant/config.yaml`: qdrant host config (storage_path: `/var/lib/qdrant/storage`, gRPC `127.0.0.1:6334`, HTTP `127.0.0.1:6333`)\n- `/etc/s6/sv/qdrant/run`: execlineb run script for qdrant s6 service (NOT yet supervised by s6-svscan)\n- `/etc/s6/sv/qdrant/dependencies.d/`: empty dependencies dir\n- `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/`: NO qdrant container rootfs here; only 3 UUID-named containers + `containers-snapshots/`, `storage-pools-volumes/`, `images/`, etc.\n- `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/containers-snapshots/`: contains snapshotted container data (qdrant old metadata may be here)\n- `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/btrfs-pool/storage-pools-volumes/`: contains qdrant volume metadata\n- `/run/service/`: s6-svscan service directory — qdrant must be linked here to be supervised\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/mutation_engine.rs`: `dispatch_rovs_commands_method` — now uses `StateEngine::method_call(\"rovs_commands\", ...)` directly\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/lib.rs`: uncommitted — removed deprecated OVS imports, trait impl, re-exports\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/main.rs`: uncommitted — cleaned daemon references\n- `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/routing_dispatch.rs`: routing dispatch (new)\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/routing.rs`: routing plugin (new)\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/gemma_brain.rs`: **deleted** — fully removed\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/mod.rs`: removed `gemma_brain`, added `routing`\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs`: removed `gemma_brain_schema`, added `routing_schema`\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/cognitive_mcp.rs`: collection name `repomix_rag` → `repos_lsp_rust_voyage_4_large`\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/incus.rs`: retry on empty container name\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/large_language_model.rs`: removed brand-brain fallback\n- `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/netmaker.rs`: async/sync mismatch bug\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/identity_source.rs`: **new** (untracked) — container identity resolution\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/interceptor.rs`: expanded with identity_source integration\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/qdrant_shuttle.rs`: added `find_collection` helper; DEFAULT_QDRANT_URL = `http://127.0.0.1:6334` (gRPC)\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/src/rag_pipeline.rs`: `list_collections` failure now non-fatal\n- `crates/op-cognitive-mcp/Cargo.toml`: added `base64` dependency\n- `crates/op-web/src/wireguard.rs`: removed manual `config_check` D-Bus method, added `generate_client_config_with_psk`\n- `docs/routing-plugin-spec.md`: routing plugin spec (new)\n- `deploy/s6/gemma/run`: now uses `zcall routing derive/publish` with fallback\n- `deploy/s6/gemma/shell_up`: same zcall routing pattern\n- `deploy/s6/gemma/down`: **new** — `zcall routing uninvoke` + cache state\n- `deploy/s6/zeroclaw-routing-uigen/`: **new** deploy directory\n- `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/run`: xray REALITY egress; exits cleanly if config missing; sources xray.env\n- `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/dependencies.d/gemma`: **needs removal** — gemma replaced by routing\n- `deploy/s6/gbr-xray/dependencies.d/gbr-warp`: xray depends on gbr-warp\n- `/etc/s6/sv/gemma/down`: exists — gemma disabled at boot ✅\n- `/etc/s6/sv/ollama/down`: exists — ollama disabled at boot ✅\n- `/etc/s6/sv/ollama-srv/down`: exists — ollama-srv disabled at boot ✅\n- `/etc/s6/sv/op-cognitive-mcp/run`: env `COGNITIVE_MCP_DB_PATH=/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db`, `WG_INTERFACE=netmaker`; depends only on `dbus-session`\n- `/etc/xray/config.json`: **FIXED** ✅ — restored from backup (5872 bytes)\n- `/etc/xray/config.json.bak-20260707200129`: last working backup with Reality + NextDNS config\n- `/etc/xray/tls.crt`, `/etc/xray/tls.key`: TLS certs present\n- `/etc/ghostbridge/xray.env`: xray environment sourced by gbr-xray\n- `/dev/shm/opdbus/projections/identity_sled.json`: **empty** `{\"sleds\":[]}`\n- `/var/lib/op-dbus/cognitive.db`: CozoDB — **520K, empty**; `blobs/` dir empty\n- `/dev/sda3`: 486GB btrfs device, **67% used** (320G used, 163G free) — cleaned from 93%\n- `/home/jeremy/git/repos/qdrant/`: qdrant source repos (qdrant server + qdrant-client)","time":{"start":1783673030876,"end":1783673082295}}');
